A BLOCK-extent promoted scalar with a later string eval takes the per-site capture-alist pair (M5, `_eval_block_cells`), never the global alias `p-alias-eval-cell`: the alias wrote the cell into the original-name global, where it outlived the block (the reproducer printed `between=ok 3`, perl `u`; a `require`d file's block cell leaked into `$M4::k`).  The alias stays for a SEGMENT-extent (file-level) cell, whose lifetime is the file's.  Parser2 `_promote_captured`: `$eval_pair = $sig eq '$' && !$extent`; `_enclosing_lex_decl` + `Binder::enclosing_decl` (the eval-pair test that chose between the two) DELETED.  Probes scratch/s537b/pr/m4a.pl (the reproducer), m4b.pl (the eval WRITES the lexical; a nested block; the same name declared again after the block, as `our`), m4c.pl (recursion through the eval; a sibling block; a file `my` after the block; a `require`d file with the shape): perl -> base 23f0f917 (leaks: between=ok 3, def, k-def) -> tree = perl, except the one line perl's "Variable is not available" rule decides (`sub get { eval '$k' }` called after its block: perl undef, PCL the cell -- pre-existing, DECIDED s504c's note; base and tree alike).  Guard Pl/t/capture-binder-01.t row 14 (fails on the base).

